                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I remember 2004 as a kid. I entered blockbuster. The smell of all the cases, seeing all the XBOX games I could rent. It was a golden age of gaming, where developers were passionate, games were made with effort and fully. No microtransactions, or endless DLC. Rented this game, and I couldn't get past the first level at the time.\n\nJump 20+ years to now. To my amazement and happiness this game was on steam. Nabbed it during the sale, and completed something that my childhood self couldn't. A sense of pride, nostalgia and emotion of a time when life was simpler and right.\n\nNow the game:\n\nIt's a early 2000s shooter. Meaning no minimap, linear, aim bot enemies, artificial difficulty and can finish in 4-5 hours. The gunplay is solid, enemies go down fast, but you can't take many hits. The story is a generic 2000s era (and i say this as a good thing) action blockbuster to stop the bad guys and save the world. \n\nCharacters.. they aren't explained and the story other than stop the bomb made little sense. \n\nNegatives: The guns you start the level with is what you end with. You cannot pickup enemy weapons. There are no checkpoints, so if you die you have to redo the level. Game is pretty short at 4-5 hours.\n\nHonestly it's a great 2000s era blast and can 100% recommend. During sales it's literally $1 so there is nothing to lose. It's a great game to kill a weekend with.",
